note Translated from go src/time/format.go, parseSignedOffset (lines 1508 to 1523).

note leadingInt in Go returns (x uint64, rem string, err error); err is set only when the digits overflow. If there are no leading digits it gives x = 0 and rem = s with no error.
type Leading_int
    field x as a Nat
    field rem as Text

to leading_int s
    given s is Text
    produces a Leading_int
    fails with LeadingIntOverflow

to parse_signed_offset value
    given value is Text
    produces an Int

    note UNCLEAR: Go's value[0] panics on an empty string (callers never pass one); the doc has no panic and does not say what an out-of-range index does, and adding `expect count of value is at least 1` would invent a precondition the original does not state, so none is written
    note GAP: byte indexing and slicing of Text - `byte 0 of value` and `slice of value from 1 until count of value` are invented; the doc has no Text indexing or substring form
    note UNCLEAR: whether `count of` a Text is in bytes or characters; Go's len is bytes
    let sign be byte 0 of value
    note UNCLEAR: no character literal in the doc; '-' and '+' are written as one-character Text, which would then compare a Byte with Text, against "is compares like with like only"
    if sign is not "-" and sign is not "+"
        give back 0
    let rest be slice of value from 1 until count of value
    note WORKAROUND: Go tests `err != nil` with a value in hand; here the failure is handled and turned into the same result 0, which needs a handle block wrapping the rest of the body
    handle
        let parsed be try leading_int rest
        note fail if nothing consumed by leading_int
        if rem of parsed is rest
            give back 0
        if x of parsed is more than 23
            give back 0
        give back count of value - count of rem of parsed
    on failure LeadingIntOverflow
        give back 0
